# Q_k Theory Milestone 1

**Branch:** CM Structural Computation — Theory  
**Date:** 2026-09-28  
**Scope:** bounded conditioned-count queries, Fourier/marginal equivalence, rank, indistinguishability, reconstruction thresholds, first structured-class results, and priority audit.

## Executive result

The elementary linear theory of the bounded conditioned-count operator is now clean and complete. The core facts are correct, but the Fourier/marginal equivalence and dimension count are not new: they are classical/known in equivalent form in contingency-table and Fourier literature. The mathematically useful outcome is therefore not to present those facts as the paper's novelty, but to use them as the ambient quotient theory and move to **class-specific injectivity and persistent representations**.

A nontrivial structured-class result obtained in this pass is an exact threshold theorem for fixed-bipartition GF(2)-rank classes: rank at most 1 has reconstruction threshold `max(p,q)`, while rank at most 2 already has the unrestricted worst-case threshold `p+q`. This creates a sharp rank-1/rank-2 discontinuity relevant to the artifact program.

