# 4. Theorem B — rank and exact-k redundancy

Let

\[
V_{\le k}
=\operatorname{span}\{\chi_T:|T|\le k\}.
\]

By (A1), every query row lies in `V_{<=k}`. Conversely,

\[
q_{T,1^T}(x)=\prod_{i\in T}x_i,
\]

and the square-free monomials of degree at most `k` are linearly independent as functions on the cube. Therefore

\[
\boxed{
\operatorname{rowspan}(Q_k)=V_{\le k}
}
\]

and

\[
\boxed{
\operatorname{rank}(Q_k)
=d_{n,k}
:=\sum_{j=0}^{k}\binom nj.
}
\tag{B1}
\]

### Exactly k coordinates already suffice

Let `Q_k^=` denote the workload containing all assignments on all subsets `S` with exactly `|S|=k`. If `T subseteq S`, `|S|=k`, then

\[
Q(f;T,a)
=\sum_{b\in\{0,1\}^{S\setminus T}}Q(f;S,a\cup b).
\]

Hence

\[
\operatorname{rowspan}(Q_k^=)
=
\operatorname{rowspan}(Q_k),
\]

so exact-`k` and at-most-`k` query families have the same rank `d_{n,k}`.

