# 5. Theorem C — complete k-indistinguishability characterization

Define

\[
f\sim_k g
\iff
Q_k f=Q_k g.
\]

Then, over `R` or `Q`,

\[
\boxed{
f\sim_k g
\iff
\widehat f(T)=\widehat g(T)\quad\forall |T|\le k
\iff
f-g\in V_{>k}.
}
\tag{C1}
\]

Thus

\[
\ker Q_k
=
\operatorname{span}\{\chi_T:|T|>k\}.
\]

The quotient `F^{2^n}/ker(Q_k)` has dimension `d_{n,k}`. Passing from `k` to `k+1` adds exactly

\[
\binom n{k+1}
\]

independent linear degrees of information.

For Boolean-valued functions, a fiber is the intersection of an affine Fourier coset with the Boolean hypercube of truth tables. Fiber sizes need not be uniform.

