# 10. Adaptive sequences of restrictions

A sequence of at most `t` coordinate restrictions ends in a partial assignment `(S,a)` with `|S|<=t`. Conversely every such partial assignment can be realized by a sequence of restrictions.

Thus, if the requested outputs are conditioned model counts (including any intermediate prefixes), the persistent information content of arbitrary adaptive restriction sequences of length at most `t` is still exactly `Q_t`.

Adaptivity changes which query is selected next; it does not enlarge the set of possible count functionals beyond the bounded marginal family.

